  data:  # 3b33
    kind: work_item  # 3b33
    title: "scala: a call on a bare PROJECT object or companion (Factory.make()) is never resolved -- Tier 1 leaves it external with no hint and no linker binds it (sbt 2,564 / lila 2,779 un-hinted edges)"  # 3b33
    status: todo_hard  # 3b33
    priority: 2  # 3b33
    parent:  # 3b33
    tags:  # 3b33
    - scala  # 3b33
    - analysis_quality  # 3b33
    isbefore: []  # 3b33
    duplicate_of: []  # 3b33
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 3b33
    pr_ref:  # 3b33
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-01 while sizing WI-gokop-nudub-zunal-zibij-fuvad-libot-bituk-visid (branch jgstern-agent/feat/gokop-scala-inferred-receivers, not yet integrated).\n\nWHAT. A method call whose receiver is a PROJECT object or companion named bare -- `Factory.make()`, `Utils.foo(x)` -- is never resolved by scala.py and is left `scala:external:0-0:<m>:unresolved` with no receiver_type_hint. The name is not in var_types, static_owner_module (WI-kilap) returns None for a project type by design (no module to write), and no type-qualified lookup is attempted. A full run_behavior_map on a one-file fixture (object Factory { def make(): FileWriter }, called as Factory.make() in another object of the same file) leaves the edge unresolved after every linker as well.\n\nSIZE (WI-gokop's sizing instrument: un-hinted external method-call edges classified by the syntax that bound the receiver, on the WI-gokop branch): receiver is a bare capitalised name that is a project class/object/trait and no binder in scope takes it -- sbt 2,564 of 14,341 un-hinted edges (17.9%), lila 2,779 of 37,100 (7.5%). The same bucket also holds library statics (sbt 1,245 / lila 1,025) that WI-kilap already slots and that are NOT this item.\n\nNOT MEASURED: how many of these the type-qualified path would bind correctly. Same-named objects in different packages are common (lila: 74 files declare a class Env; objects too), and scala symbols are name-keyed (WI-niriz), so a fix must refuse a bind the file's imports/package contradict (the WI-tipoh _import_names_elsewhere check WI-gokop reuses), and must count newly-RESOLVED edges by owner, not hints (PR #892's lesson).\n\nFIX SHAPE (not designed): in the call branch, when receiver_name is capitalised, unbound by any lexical binder and _is_project_type(...) holds, try the type-qualified lookup with type_name=receiver_name before the external branch; WI-gokop's _ScalaReceiverTyper._owner already treats such a name as an owner for registry lookups."  # 3b33
    fields: {}  # 3b33
